    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, all tests green). \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `displayName` field for owners, formatted as `LastName, FirstName` from the stored names.\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` schema. Since `OwnerDto` is generated from this spec, this produces a `displayName` field (with getter/setter) on the DTO returned by both `POST /api/owners` (201 response) and `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` on `toOwnerDto` that populates `displayName` via an expression: `owner.getLastName() + \", \" + owner.getFirstName()`.\n\nBecause the existing responders (`RespondWithOwnerCreated`, `RespondWithOwner`) already map the entity through `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`, no changes to the OfficeFloor pipeline or function classes were needed \u2014 the derived field flows through automatically on create and read.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreComputesDisplayName` (creates an owner with `firstName=John`, then reads back `$.displayName == \"LastName, John\"`) passes, along with the rest of the suite.",
